From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:23:15 +0000
Subject: fix: key host-less zoom levels on the URL without its fragment

HostZoomMap keys per-host zoom levels by net::GetHostOrSpecFromURL() of
the frame's last committed URL, which is the full spec when the URL has
no host (file:, data:, about:). A same-document navigation that only
changes the fragment on such a page therefore changed the key: the
stored level was no longer found, GetZoomLevel() reported the default
while the renderer kept the old zoom factor, and the next zoom step was
computed from the default. Strip the fragment in
GetURLForRenderFrameHostPtr(), which every zoom-keying call site goes
through.

Upstreamed at https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8467669

diff --git a/content/browser/host_zoom_map_impl.cc b/content/browser/host_zoom_map_impl.cc
index c321160361ca8ad9bce5f1bd583231825a87e030..1d231545f72a37fb64cc71da17e3b3141496bdf7 100644
--- a/content/browser/host_zoom_map_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/host_zoom_map_impl.cc
@@ -55,8 +55,12 @@ GURL GetURLForRenderFrameHostPtr(const RenderFrameHost* rfh) {
   // If a user lands on an error page, and then modifies the zoom level, it
   // should be attributed to the error-page host and not the page they were
   // trying to reach.
-  return rfh->IsErrorDocument() ? GURL(kUnreachableWebDataURL)
-                                : rfh->GetLastCommittedURL();
+  if (rfh->IsErrorDocument()) {
+    return GURL(kUnreachableWebDataURL);
+  }
+  // Zoom levels for URLs without a host are keyed by spec; drop the fragment
+  // so that same-document navigations keep the key.
+  return rfh->GetLastCommittedURL().GetWithoutRef();
 }
 
 std::string GetHostFromProcessFrame(RenderFrameHostImpl* rfh) {
